1
00:00:02,628 --> 00:00:05,880
Fellow warriors,
this is Sheldor the Conqueror.

2
00:00:06,048 --> 00:00:07,882
We are about to enter Atzel's fortress.

3
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:11,886
Now, this is a long run,
so let's do another bladder check.

4
00:00:13,972 --> 00:00:17,975
All right, Barry, we'll wait for you again,
but you really should see a doctor.

5
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:20,728
[BANGING NEARBY]

6
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:24,899
Sheldor is AFK.

7
00:00:29,196 --> 00:00:31,614
Penny, are you experiencing
some sort of difficulty?

8
00:00:31,782 --> 00:00:34,283
Yes, I can't get my stupid door open.

9
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:38,621
You appear to have put your car key
in the door lock. Are you aware of that?

10
00:00:39,248 --> 00:00:40,790
Yeah.

11
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,042
All right, then.

12
00:00:44,503 --> 00:00:47,421
PENNY:
Damn it, damn it, damn it.

13
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:50,633
Would it be possible for you
to do this a little more quietly?

14
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:54,554
-l can't get the damn key out.
-That's not surprising.

15
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:58,099
That Baldwin lock on your door uses
traditional edge-mounted cylinders...

16
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:02,395
...whereas the key for your Volkswagen
uses a center-cylinder system.

17
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:05,481
Thank you, Sheldon.

18
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:08,192
You're welcome.

19
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:12,238
Point of inquiry: Why did you
put your car key in the door lock?

20
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:14,490
I'll tell you why.
Today I had an audition.

21
00:01:14,658 --> 00:01:17,577
It took me two hours to get there.
I waited an hour for my turn.

22
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:20,913
Before I could start, they told me
I look too Midwest for the part.

23
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:23,291
Too Midwest.
What the hell does that even mean?

24
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:28,254
The American Midwest was mostly settled
by Scandinavian and Germanic peoples...

25
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:31,132
-...who have characteristic facial--
-l know what it means.

26
00:01:32,593 --> 00:01:35,344
God, l have been in L.A.
for almost two years now.

27
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:38,681
I haven't gotten a single acting job.
I've accomplished nothing.

28
00:01:38,849 --> 00:01:41,934
Haven't gotten a raise at work.
Haven't even had sex in six months.

29
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:47,064
And when l was walking up those stairs
a fly flew in my mouth and l ate it.

30
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:51,027
Well, actually, insects are a dietary staple
in many cultures.

31
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:52,528
They're almost pure protein.

32
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:56,032
Oh, son of a bitch.

33
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:58,576
The condensation on your frozen foods...

34
00:01:58,744 --> 00:02:01,370
...weakened the structural integrity
of the bag.

35
00:02:05,876 --> 00:02:09,170
But returning to your key conundrum,
you should call a locksmith.

36
00:02:09,338 --> 00:02:11,213
-Have him open the door for you.
-l did.

37
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:13,507
He said he'll get here when he gets here.

38
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:17,261
You're frustrated because he phrased
his reply in a meaningless tautology?

39
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:21,474
No. l am frustrated
because l am a failure at everything...

40
00:02:21,642 --> 00:02:24,894
...and my breath smells like fly.

41
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,312
[CRYING]

42
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:29,982
There, there.

43
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:40,201
Would you prefer to wait
in our apartment?

44
00:02:40,369 --> 00:02:43,829
No, l'd rather sit on this freezing floor,
sobbing like a 3-year-old.

45
00:02:44,581 --> 00:02:46,457
All right, then.

46
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:49,460
For God's sake.

47
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:54,840
Just when I think l've gotten
the hang of sarcasm.

48
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:22,076
Make yourself comfortable.

49
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:24,412
Not there.

50
00:03:25,789 --> 00:03:27,039
[SCOFFS]

51
00:03:53,734 --> 00:03:55,693
Sheldor is back online.

52
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:58,612
Sheldor?

53
00:03:59,281 --> 00:04:00,948
The Conqueror.

54
00:04:02,159 --> 00:04:03,200
What are you doing?

55
00:04:04,703 --> 00:04:05,911
AFK.

56
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:10,374
I'm playing "Age of Conan,"
an online multiplayer game...

57
00:04:10,542 --> 00:04:13,711
...set in the universe of Robert E. Howard's
Conan the Barbarian.

58
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:15,546
Oh.

59
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:19,383
Sheldor back online.

60
00:04:19,843 --> 00:04:22,428
-What's AFK?
-AFK.

61
00:04:24,723 --> 00:04:27,183
Away from keyboard.

62
00:04:27,851 --> 00:04:29,226
Oh, l see.

63
00:04:30,187 --> 00:04:32,313
What does that stand for?

64
00:04:36,735 --> 00:04:39,236
Oh, l see.

65
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:42,907
Yes, but what does it stand for?

66
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:59,131
And just click on the enchanted boots
to put them on.

67
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:02,510
I don't know.
Can I see them in another color?

68
00:05:03,261 --> 00:05:04,720
Just click on them.

69
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:09,600
Now, congratulations,
you are now a level-three warrior.

70
00:05:09,768 --> 00:05:12,812
-What's going on?
-Guess what? I'm a level-three warrior.

71
00:05:13,939 --> 00:05:16,732
Do you know there are groceries
outside of your apartment?

72
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,317
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Shh.

73
00:05:19,194 --> 00:05:23,447
I only bring it up because your ice cream's
melting and it's starting to attract wildlife.

74
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:26,659
Uh-huh. Do l stay in the jungle
or go towards the beach?

75
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:29,954
-Doesn't matter, you're looking for treasure.
-Okay.

76
00:05:32,249 --> 00:05:34,667
-Wait, where are you going?
-Go ahead. You're okay.

77
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:38,087
If you run into crocodiles,
just kick them with your boots.

78
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:42,633
Wanna catch me up?

79
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:46,762
Well, uh, let's see. She attempted
to open her apartment with her car key...

80
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:50,349
...because her face is overly Midwestern.
Uh....

81
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:53,143
She hasn't had sex in six months.

82
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:55,646
And she ate a fly.

83
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:58,899
Uh-huh.

84
00:05:59,693 --> 00:06:01,986
Seriously, six months?

85
00:06:02,153 --> 00:06:04,196
Oh, my God, a treasure chest. I'm rich.

86
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:07,992
Level three and she thinks she's rich.

87
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:13,205
What a newb.

88
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:18,252
Okay, we're all set.

89
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:20,129
Let her rip.

90
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:35,311
-Hi.
-Hey, check it out.

91
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:37,229
It's just corn starch and water.

92
00:06:40,692 --> 00:06:43,319
They make up a non-Newtonian fluid
which is liquid...

93
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:46,113
...but solid under the percussive action
of the speaker.

94
00:06:46,281 --> 00:06:49,533
That's what makes it get all funky.

95
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:53,787
Yeah, okay.

96
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:55,831
Listen, l need to talk to Sheldon.

97
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:02,796
No, that's what she said, Sheldon.

98
00:07:03,465 --> 00:07:06,884
Okay, I bought the game and l've been
exploring the lsland of Tortage.

99
00:07:07,052 --> 00:07:08,969
I can't figure how to pass the guard.

100
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:11,847
-Do you have the enchanted sword?
-l have a bronze dagger.

101
00:07:12,015 --> 00:07:13,891
You can't slay the guard with a dagger.

102
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:17,227
Lord, it's like the car key
in your apartment door all over again.

103
00:07:17,395 --> 00:07:20,314
-How do I get the sword?
-Have you been to the Temple of Mitra?

104
00:07:20,482 --> 00:07:23,192
-ls that the place on the hill with the priest?
-No, it's--

105
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:24,985
Oh, for God's sakes, give me.

106
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:26,820
Thank you. I really appreciate this.

107
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:28,906
You have to learn to do these things.

108
00:07:29,074 --> 00:07:31,367
Don't patronize me. Just get the sword.

109
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:35,537
What the frak?

110
00:07:36,498 --> 00:07:39,541
Beats me.
They were playing all last night too.

111
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:43,045
It's like some kind
of weird comic-book crossover.

112
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:46,882
Like if Hulk
were dating Peppermint Patty.

113
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:49,218
I always thought Peppermint Patty
was a lesbian.

114
00:07:49,386 --> 00:07:50,552
No, that's Marcie.

115
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,180
Peppermint Patty's just athletic.

116
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:56,016
There you go, one enchanted sword.

117
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:59,311
All right, give me, give me.
I wanna kill the guard captain.

118
00:08:03,775 --> 00:08:05,901
That girl needs to get a life.

119
00:08:15,078 --> 00:08:16,412
[KNOCKlNG ON DOOR]

120
00:08:18,415 --> 00:08:19,999
Sheldon.

121
00:08:26,089 --> 00:08:29,216
-Sheldon.
-Danger. Danger.

122
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:30,884
No danger, it's me, Penny.

123
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:34,221
Listen, l got to level 25
and reached Purple Lotus Swamp, right?

124
00:08:34,389 --> 00:08:36,056
-You're in my bedroom.
-Yeah.

125
00:08:36,725 --> 00:08:40,269
-Leonard gave me an emergency key.
-People can't be in my bedroom.

126
00:08:40,437 --> 00:08:43,689
-Can we go talk in the living room?
-l'm not wearing pajama bottoms.

127
00:08:45,316 --> 00:08:47,860
-Why not?
-l spilled grape juice.

128
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:49,695
Well, wear different pajamas.

129
00:08:49,863 --> 00:08:52,740
Can't wear different pajamas.
These are my Monday pajamas.

130
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:55,659
Penny, people cannot be in my bedroom.

131
00:08:56,036 --> 00:08:59,121
Just tell me, is it too soon
to join a quest to the Black Castle?

132
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:02,332
You were invited on a quest
to the Black Castle?

133
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:06,545
By some guys in Budapest. l'm just not
sure it's the right move for my character.

134
00:09:06,921 --> 00:09:09,673
Of course it's not. You're only a level 25.

135
00:09:09,841 --> 00:09:13,343
These Hungarians are just using you
for dragon fodder.

136
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:18,474
Really? Boy, you'd think you could trust
a horde of Hungarian Barbarians.

137
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:22,519
SHELDON:
Please, Penny, enough. l have to sleep.

138
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:27,649
PENNY:
Okay, well, you were great. Thanks.

139
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:33,489
Oh. Listen, don't go in Sheldon's room.
He's not wearing bottoms.

140
00:09:39,537 --> 00:09:40,579
[KNOCKlNG]

141
00:09:40,747 --> 00:09:43,165
Sheldon, you wanna catch me up again?

142
00:09:46,336 --> 00:09:48,253
People, l am very busy today.

143
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:51,840
I realize that, but it is your job
as head of the department...

144
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:54,093
...to mediate all intra-departmental
disputes.

145
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,512
University Policy Manual, Chapter 4,
subsection 2:

146
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:59,181
"Mediation
of lntra-departmental Disputes."

147
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:00,349
[SCOFFS]

148
00:10:00,517 --> 00:10:02,017
Fine.

149
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:05,854
Dr. Winkle, what colorful name
did you call Dr. Cooper this time?

150
00:10:06,523 --> 00:10:08,357
Dr. Dumb-ass.

151
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:13,028
Dr. Cooper, Dr. Winkle apologizes.

152
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:14,613
-No, she doesn't.
-No, I don't.

153
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:19,701
Here's the problem. I was clearly signed up
to use the mainframe in Buckman 204...

154
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:22,788
...and Dr. Winkle just ripped
the sign-up sheet off the wall.

155
00:10:22,956 --> 00:10:25,374
It wasn't an official sign-up sheet.
He printed it...

156
00:10:25,542 --> 00:10:29,044
...and he put his name down
on every slot for the next six months.

157
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:31,797
If it is a crime to ensure
the university's resources...

158
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:34,758
...are not being squandered
chasing subatomic wild geese...

159
00:10:34,926 --> 00:10:36,593
...then l plead guilty.

160
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:38,428
[PHONE RINGlNG]

161
00:10:39,973 --> 00:10:41,056
Oh, Penny.

162
00:10:41,224 --> 00:10:44,017
-You need to get that, Dr. Cooper?
-God, no.

163
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:46,854
Don't turn it off. You might miss
your call from Nobel...

164
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:50,732
...letting you know you've been nominated
as dumb-ass laureate of the year.

165
00:10:51,234 --> 00:10:55,279
Oh, yeah, well,
you wouldn't even be nominated.

166
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:04,246
I have a series of important multi-loop
calculations and simulations to run.

167
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:06,373
She's reducing irrelevant data,
making a mock--

168
00:11:06,541 --> 00:11:07,583
[PHONE RINGS]

169
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,209
Excuse me.

170
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:11,336
Gablehauser.

171
00:11:12,547 --> 00:11:13,589
It's for you.

172
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:18,594
Hello?

173
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:21,430
Penny, this is not a good time.

174
00:11:21,598 --> 00:11:25,434
No, l told you, you're not prepared
for the Sanctum of Burning Souls.

175
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:31,231
You need to be in a group of at least five
and one should be a level 35 healer.

176
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:33,025
No, l can't log on and help you.

177
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:36,987
We'll talk when l get home.

178
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:44,786
I'm not getting the computing time,
am I?

179
00:11:45,288 --> 00:11:46,955
Dumb-ass.

180
00:11:51,211 --> 00:11:53,629
Leonard, you have to do something
about Penny.

181
00:11:53,796 --> 00:11:56,840
She is interfering with my sleep.
She is interfering with my work.

182
00:11:57,008 --> 00:11:59,301
If I had another significant aspect
of my life...

183
00:11:59,469 --> 00:12:01,845
...I'm sure she'd be interfering
with that too.

184
00:12:03,306 --> 00:12:06,391
Why should l do something?
You introduced her to online gaming.

185
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:10,395
Well, yes, but you're the one
who said hello to her when she moved in.

186
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:14,483
If you'd simply restrained yourself,
none of this would be happening.

187
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:19,321
-Well, just tell her to leave you alone.
-l did. l told her. I texted her.

188
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:21,365
I sent out a very emphatic Twitter.

189
00:12:21,532 --> 00:12:25,327
I changed my Facebook status to "Sheldon
wishes Penny would leave him alone."

190
00:12:25,495 --> 00:12:27,204
I don't know what else to do.

191
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:29,998
Well, what am l supposed to do?

192
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:32,501
If you don't figure something out,
I warn you...

193
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:36,004
...I shall become very difficult
to live with.

194
00:12:37,048 --> 00:12:42,010
You mean, up until now we've been
experiencing the happy fun-time Sheldon?

195
00:12:42,178 --> 00:12:44,638
-Yes.
-l'll go talk to her.

196
00:12:46,349 --> 00:12:48,892
No, Fritz, l need you on my flank.

197
00:12:49,227 --> 00:12:50,352
No, l don't know German.

198
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:51,687
[SPEAKlNG INDISTINCTLY]

199
00:12:52,772 --> 00:12:53,897
[KNOCKlNG ON DOOR]

200
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,526
-Hey, Penny?
-Busy.

201
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:00,362
Yeah, I see that.
Shouldn't you be at work?

202
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:01,905
I don't work on Mondays.

203
00:13:02,365 --> 00:13:04,116
It's Thursday.

204
00:13:06,369 --> 00:13:10,580
-Listen, Penny--
-Ugh. Queen Penelope AFK. What?

205
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,626
Okay. Uh....

206
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:15,919
Here's the thing.

207
00:13:16,087 --> 00:13:20,340
Um, sometimes people, good people,
you know, they start playing these games.

208
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:24,553
They find themselves, through no fault
of their own, you know, kind of addicted.

209
00:13:24,721 --> 00:13:27,597
Yeah, get to the point.
I'm about to level up here.

210
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:31,059
If a person doesn't have a sense
of achievement in their real life...

211
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:35,647
...it's easy to lose themselves in a world
where a false sense of accomplishment--

212
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:39,234
Yeah, jabber, jabber, jabber.
Okay, boys, Queen Penelope's back online.

213
00:13:40,737 --> 00:13:42,321
Penny, you've got...

214
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,573
...Cheetos in your hair.

215
00:13:46,409 --> 00:13:48,368
Oh, thanks.

216
00:13:52,457 --> 00:13:53,874
Wow.

217
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:03,258
LEONARD:
Hey, Penny, it's me again, Leonard.

218
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:04,843
PENNY:
Leonard, l said, not now.

219
00:14:05,011 --> 00:14:07,262
LEONARD: I'm just a little concerned
about you and--

220
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:08,764
PENNY:
l said, not now.

221
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:10,849
LEONARD:
Okay, maybe later.

222
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:14,770
-Hey, guys.
-Hey.

223
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:17,939
-Hey, what's with him?
-Penny's been keeping him up at night.

224
00:14:20,026 --> 00:14:21,318
Me too.

225
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:27,657
But probably in a different way.

226
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:31,286
She's really hooked on "Age of Conan."
She's playing non-stop.

227
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:33,455
Oh, yes, online gaming addiction.

228
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:37,793
There's nothing worse than having
that multiplayer monkey on your back.

229
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:42,130
-Sheldon, wake up.
-Danger, danger.

230
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:46,134
Afternoon, men. Sheldon.

231
00:14:47,512 --> 00:14:49,805
Oh, yeah, well, your attempt
at juvenilizing me...

232
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:55,143
...by excluding me from the set of adult
males just-- Oh, I'm too tired to do this.

233
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:59,648
Right. l heard you've been pulling
all-nighters with Middle-Earth Barbie.

234
00:15:00,441 --> 00:15:04,403
She comes into my room.
No one's supposed to be in my room.

235
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:07,239
I would postulate
she's escaping into the online world...

236
